 ## Overview
-Half-Space Field Generation creates a binary volume mask by assigning values to voxels based on a spatial or level-set condition, effectively gating simulation or rendering computations [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from continuous implicit primitives by discretizing the domain boundary into a hard binary mask rather than evaluating a smooth scalar field for isosurface extraction [G]. This method restricts physical simulation (such as pressure solving or force application) to active regions, ignoring empty space like air [S2, unofficial].
